# go-adk-q Coding Rules
# Auto-loaded by Cursor IDE from repo root

## Project identity
# Stack: Go 1.24 · google.golang.org/adk v1.2.0 · Bubbletea TUI · multi-provider failover
# Module: go-adk-q
# Entry points: main.go (ADK server), cmd/tui/main.go (TUI binary)

## Hard rules (imperative)

Always put ALL new agent definitions in main.go, not in separate files.
Always use `m` (the failover chain variable) as Model in every new agent.
Always add both `json:"name"` and `jsonschema:"Description."` tags to FunctionTool args struct fields.
Always include `exitlooptool.New()` in the Tools of any LoopAgent sub-agent that should exit early.
Always use `mustOK(err, "create agent_name")` immediately after llmagent.New/sequentialagent.New/etc.
Always use unique OutputKey values across all stages in a SequentialAgent pipeline.
Always create new provider packages in model/<providerName>/ with Config struct + ConfigFromEnv() + NewModel().
Always return nil (not an error) from NewModel() when the API key env var is unset.
Always register new providers in model/catalog/catalog.go KnownModels list.
Always use `localskilltoolset.New(...)` — never the upstream google.golang.org/adk/tool/skilltoolset directly.

Never import github.com/firebase/genkit outside model/oaibridge/bridge.go.
Never assign Tools or Toolsets to Groq or NVIDIA provider-specific agents.
Never deploy with ECHO_FALLBACK_ENABLED=1 — the echo model returns static text.
Never use a raw provider model (groqLLM, nvidiaLLM, etc.) in a production agent; always use m.
Never use `utils`, `helpers`, or `common` as package names.
Never name two OutputKeys the same across stages of a SequentialAgent.
Never call os.Exit in agent handlers or tool implementations.

## Terminology
# Say: provider (not: backend, vendor)
# Say: LlmAgent (not: LLM agent, chat agent)
# Say: FunctionTool (not: tool function, action)
# Say: SkillToolset (not: skill plugin, tool plugin)
# Say: failover chain (not: fallback chain, retry chain)
# Say: session state (not: agent state, memory)
# Say: oaibridge (not: OpenAI bridge, GenKit bridge)
# Say: SKILL.md (not: skill file, plugin file)

## FunctionTool skeleton
# ```go
# type myArgs struct {
#     Input string `json:"input" jsonschema:"Description for the LLM."`
# }
# type myResult struct { Output string `json:"output"` }
# func myHandler(_ tool.Context, a myArgs) (myResult, error) {
#     if a.Input == "" { return myResult{}, fmt.Errorf("input required") }
#     return myResult{Output: a.Input}, nil
# }
# func NewMyTool() tool.Tool {
#     t, err := functiontool.New(functiontool.Config{Name:"my_tool", Description:"..."}, myHandler)
#     if err != nil { panic(fmt.Sprintf("NewMyTool: %v", err)) }
#     return t
# }
# ```

## New agent skeleton
# ```go
# myAgent, err := llmagent.New(llmagent.Config{
#     Name:        "my_agent",
#     Model:       m,
#     Description: "Routing hint for root agent — be specific.",
#     Instruction: "System prompt. Reference state with {key}.",
#     OutputKey:   "my_output",
#     Tools:       []tool.Tool{tools.NewWeatherTool()},
#     Toolsets:    agentToolsets,
# })
# mustOK(err, "create my_agent")
# ```

## Key file paths
# main.go               — all agent definitions
# tools/tools.go        — FunctionTools
# model/failover/       — failover chain
# model/oaibridge/      — only Genkit import
# cmd/tui/main.go       — TUI entry
# tool/skilltoolset/    — schema-patched SkillToolset
# skills/               — SKILL.md library
# docs/ai-memory/       — AI context files
# AGENTS.md             — full coding instructions
# llms-full.txt         — full RAG context

## Testing
# go test ./...         — all unit tests
# make test             — via Makefile
# Skip provider tests when API key is unset:
#   if os.Getenv("GROQ_API_KEY") == "" { t.Skip("...") }
